NAME
	movement

SYNOPSYS
	<direction>
	go <direction>

DESCRIPTION
	The location you are in may display one or more obvious exits you can
	travel to, such as "north", or "up". To move in that direction, enter
	the word (e.g. "north", but "go north" also works). Even easier, the
	standard directions can be abbreviated, e.g. "n" for north, or "sw"
	for southwest.

	Since you are a packet on a network "upstream" or "downstream" will
	be more common, than say east or west, and those directions can be 
	also abbreviated, as "us" and "ds" respectively.
